      "writtenOn": "2018-02-28T21:30:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t have GPIO_USB_C0_5V_EN to indicate OTG is enabled. We can probably find an unused floating GPIO pin as GPIO_USB_C0_5V_EN and turn it on when OTG is enabled. Then we don\u0027t need to introduce a new config here - the whole purpose is to work around usb_charger.c. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "d7d3841b_485c3913",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2676,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2681,
        "endChar": 0
      },
